---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND } from '../config';
const UPDATED = 'October 12, 2026';
---

<Base
  title={`Acceptable Use Policy | ${BRAND}`}
  description={`What you may and may not do with ${BRAND}'s AI resume rewrite feature: honest use, prohibited misuse, and prohibited content including sexually explicit material.`}
  path="/acceptable-use"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

    <p>
      This policy covers the AI rewrite feature (and every other part of {BRAND}). It is part of our
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. Breaking it can lead to refused service, quota or account
      suspension, and — where required — reports to the relevant authorities.
    </p>

    <h2>What the AI rewrite is for</h2>
    <p>
      One thing only: helping <b>you</b> present <b>your own real experience</b> in the wording of a job
      description you are genuinely considering. The tool rephrases your facts; it never invents new ones,
      and you're not allowed to make it try.
    </p>

    <h2>Prohibited content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Sexually explicit or NSFW content.</b> Requesting that the AI rewrite generate, describe, or
        promote sexually explicit, pornographic, or otherwise NSFW material is prohibited. The rewrite
        feature is strictly for professional job-application documents.
      </li>
      <li>Content that is illegal in your jurisdiction or ours, or that infringes anyone's rights.</li>
      <li>Hateful, harassing, discriminatory, or violent content.</li>
      <li>Malware, phishing text, or content designed to deceive security systems.</li>
      <li>
        Other people's resumes or private data you don't have permission to use — including scraped or
        purchased personal data.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prohibited uses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Fabricating qualifications.</b> Using the rewrite to invent degrees, employers, titles,
        certifications, or experience you don't have. The tool flags job requirements your resume can't
        support — treat those flags as stop signs, not suggestions.
      </li>
      <li>Impersonating another person or applying on someone's behalf without their consent.</li>
      <li>
        Automated abuse: bots, scrapers, mass automated requests, or any attempt to circumvent free-quota or
        credit limits (including creating multiple accounts to re-earn free quota).
      </li>
      <li>Reverse-engineering, reselling, or white-labeling the service.</li>
      <li>Using the service to build a competing dataset or to train machine-learning models.</li>
      <li>Any use that violates the law of your jurisdiction, ours, or Creem's payment policies.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Fair-use limits</h2>
    <p>
      Credits and free rewrites are for a single person's genuine job hunt. Very high request rates,
      anomalous usage patterns, or chargeback abuse may trigger automatic suspension while we take a look.
    </p>

    <h2>Enforcement</h2>
    <p>
      We may refuse a rewrite request, cap usage, suspend an account, or terminate service for violations.
      If we terminate a paid account for these reasons, unused credits are refunded at our discretion where
      the law doesn't say otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting misuse</h2>
    <p>
      Found someone using {BRAND} in violation of this policy? Email
      <a href="mailto:support@tailorresume.dev">support@tailorresume.dev</a> with details. We take fraud and
      abuse reports seriously.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
